<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_e318e1d9-88a7-4f4d-8c55-c00bf2a9ef5b"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act, except in so far as the context or
subject-matter otherwise indicates or requires:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_752c0d6a-2377-4eee-8a9c-2ffd160d7114"
id="def.employment"><b><i>employment</i></b></defterm> means
employment:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_841c0606-069c-4eec-bfad-a7bddbab7576" id="sec.4-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">under a contract of service,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_43d90c3a-cc6d-4937-b05a-213aef893169" id="sec.4-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">under a contract for services,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_0b53a9e8-dba8-4230-8f0e-bd831ad15e53" id="sec.4-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">as an agent remunerated wholly or partly by
commission.</txt></block></li></list>
</block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_3ffca70d-65aa-40c2-bf75-bcc2bbc5c71a"
id="def.output"><b><i>output</i></b></defterm>, in relation to an instrument
or apparatus, includes a reproduction of, extract from, summary of, or
paraphrase of, output from the instrument or apparatus.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_a2111917-b7fe-4770-911e-b68dd81179b3"
id="def.prohibitedpurpose"><b><i>prohibited purpose</i></b></defterm> means
any purpose connected with:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_faa7714c-9903-4300-8f54-9464e1f5b86d" id="sec.4-para1.a-oc.2">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">matters relating to employment, including:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_68956a31-1769-4221-9316-f5c73e90a4df" id="sec.4-para1.a-oc.2-para2.i">
<no>(i)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">an application for, or offer of,
employment,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_52efff16-8414-43da-81f5-57ae6f073a53"
id="sec.4-para1.a-oc.2-para2.ii">
<no>(ii)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">honesty and other matters related to
character,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_b12068ac-caa6-498e-8bd2-9a9930df9467"
id="sec.4-para1.a-oc.2-para2.iii">
<no>(iii)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">terms of employment,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_91ba65a3-c103-4f10-ace4-4e4de51ced58"
id="sec.4-para1.a-oc.2-para2.iv">
<no>(iv)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">promotion, increments and other
employment-related benefits,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_9252f5a2-514a-4c9c-9522-4ef7f62a8348" id="sec.4-para1.a-oc.2-para2.v">
<no>(v)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">transfer of employment,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_87829c72-42ac-450d-ab4c-a54fa671bb80"
id="sec.4-para1.a-oc.2-para2.vi">
<no>(vi)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">training in or for employment,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_a4292cb5-1e85-45d3-b25f-82b0bb1422d3"
id="sec.4-para1.a-oc.2-para2.vii">
<no>(vii)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">continuation of
employment,</txt></block></li></list>
</block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_bafda3d8-fa51-433b-8e50-69409a2b5b3d" id="sec.4-para1.b-oc.2">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">consideration of the acceptance of risk under a
proposal for a contract of, or policy of, insurance,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_d4c81bcc-16b3-40fc-9218-d8d33770f5c8" id="sec.4-para1.c-oc.2">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">consideration of a claim under a policy of
insurance,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_aedc2c65-8ed7-498e-a2d9-617c910510c0" id="sec.4-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">payment of compensation for loss or damage,
whether under a policy of insurance or otherwise,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_f7d71882-02e9-465a-90ef-f4b4296ed8ec" id="sec.4-para1.e">
<no>(e)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">an application for any form of financial
accommodation, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_73204478-e94f-4883-a84e-e0a868446b59" id="sec.4-para1.f">
<no>(f)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">establishing whether or not a person is guilty of
an act or omission that is punishable by a fine or
imprisonment.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></deflist>
</block>

<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 4:</b> Am 1984 No 153,
Sch 9; 1999 No 94, Sch 4.127.</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_57a0ed6f-ead3-4d1d-9d86-41c33a991877"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_adfc3c3c-4bc7-42c4-a76f-075d4ef21074"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Offences</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_38f25d94-5309-48a4-a7b9-e33ef16c2ea1"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A person is guilty of an offence against this Act
if, for any prohibited purpose:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_f38e91dc-8472-4862-880e-f718894982ac" id="sec.5-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the person uses an instrument or apparatus to
measure or monitor:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_147f4969-fc32-4a3a-a053-0954fd59f2c4"
id="sec.5-ssec.1-para1.a-para2.i">
<no>(i)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">physiological reactions of the body of another
person, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_4d435294-28ed-475f-9779-4da889c325ff"
id="sec.5-ssec.1-para1.a-para2.ii">
<no>(ii)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">elements of stress, tonal variation or vibration
in the voice of another person,</txt></block></li></list>
</block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_600b453f-d0f6-4e47-abdd-7d4f9c25a4c3" id="sec.5-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the person uses the output from an instrument or
apparatus so used by the person or another person, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_df1e6dea-8722-4efd-a1e5-ee64e902e887" id="sec.5-ssec.1-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the person uses an analysis of, or opinion as to
the effect of, any such output.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3cbedfc6-5721-44f0-ae45-9e265250592c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A person is guilty of an offence against this Act
if, for any prohibited purpose, the person requests or requires another person
to undergo an examination based on the use of an instrument or apparatus to
measure or monitor:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_2d806cf2-fdec-4d17-bf82-556320a2ee2f" id="sec.5-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">physiological reactions of the body of that other
person, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_af0e391c-6cb2-4052-94ce-02cc518e6338" id="sec.5-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">elements of stress, tonal variation or vibration
in the voice of that other person.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a021d7ef-9cf1-4df1-8788-139766badd10"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_68c59203-dd98-4bef-a6f5-7be051e8a2a8"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Output etc not admissible in evidence</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f610d80a-41ed-45a1-b8fb-516f195b28db"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subject to subsection (2), anything that is, or
purports to be:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_51bf4a44-2913-440d-8989-4f60921b9999" id="sec.6-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">output from an instrument or apparatus when used
in the commission of an offence against this Act referred to in section 5,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_bcb81211-45b4-48d7-b477-f0337b8819dd" id="sec.6-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">an analysis of, or opinion as to the effect of,
any such output,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">is inadmissible as evidence before any court or any
person or body of persons authorised by law or by consent of parties to
receive and examine evidence.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7cbd4136-f7cd-479d-9d97-9b9e86a7badb"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subsection (1) does not operate to prohibit the
production or admission in evidence, for the purpose of proving the commission
of an offence against this Act, of any output, analysis or opinion alleged to
have been used in the commission of the offence.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_442d86ac-1fe1-45a1-9f8f-a277079517ae"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The court before which proceedings for an offence
against this Act are brought may, at any stage of the proceedings and from
time to time, make an order forbidding publication of evidence that, but for
subsection (2), would be inadmissible in those proceedings, or of any report
of, or report of the substance or purport of, that
evidence.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_923adef4-e356-4bdf-ab7c-7af1a078d83b"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A person who contravenes an order made under
subsection (3) is guilty of an offence against this Act.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_d0af4924-edd9-4f5b-83d1-a2cfadfa3999"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_961014e7-bb2f-47e7-b236-5890219938f6"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Penalties</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3369c0f9-0109-4e71-85bb-ba7ed3c1ce00"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A person guilty of an offence against this Act is
liable:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_8766ebf7-aa85-43fa-9671-d6e86cf48d32" id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">in the case of a corporation&#8212;to a penalty
not exceeding 50 penalty units for a first offence and not exceeding 100
penalty units for a second or subsequent offence, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_4d3ea93f-feab-4ee8-8c19-5dad33592ce9" id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">in any other case&#8212;to a penalty not
exceeding 10 penalty units for a first offence and not exceeding 20 penalty
units for a second or subsequent offence.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_8f1b13e2-9c33-4bc0-a9dd-0a2d0d8d296e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Proceedings for an offence against this Act may
be taken before the Local Court.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e5736cc1-dd56-4e25-8ed9-3492e2bb8d0e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The court by which a person is convicted of an
offence against this Act may, by its conviction, order that:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_24d37b32-f2a4-4227-8cc4-04cf362f16ac" id="sec.7-ssec.3-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any instrument or apparatus,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_d98e9d67-32d3-4e3b-a42b-cf67a13f0cbe" id="sec.7-ssec.3-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any written or recorded output from an instrument
or apparatus, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_11eb878a-14c5-4532-9e60-ce0c03fa8df3" id="sec.7-ssec.3-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any written or recorded analysis of, or opinion
as to the effect of, output from an instrument or
apparatus,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">used in the commission of the offence and described in
the order be forfeited to the Crown and delivered, within a period specified
in the order by the person who has possession of the device, output, analysis
or opinion to a person so specified to be dealt with as the Minister thinks
fit.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 7:</b> Am 1993 No 47,
Sch 1; 1999 No 31, Sch 4.51; 2007 No 94, Sch 4.</txt></content>
</level>
</content>


